WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:15.000
Compare approval policies across profit, credit losses and cash.
10,000 synthetic applications; a common 39-month runoff horizon.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Aggressive earns about $396k, but minimum cash falls to -$1.49m.
Conservative meets the base limits: about $48k profit and $147k minimum cash.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:45.000
Starting equity of $1.25m makes Balanced eligible and recommended.
Profit stays about $294k; minimum cash reaches $54k. Equity has no modeled financing cost.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:00.000
At 2x lifetime defaults, Conservative loses about $11.6k.
It is a diagnostic only: no eligible policy produces positive operating profit.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Loan, debt, cash, cohort and simplified-equity schedules reconcile.
Principal collections are not revenue; charge-offs are not a second cash payment.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:30.000
The brief records the recommendation, policy tradeoffs and applied inputs.
